{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"58db2c2382ec511a","name":"card_unit_pzl_11","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/units/card_unit_pzl_11","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"PZL P.11","text":"Your Exile cards cost 1 less.","flavorText":"The PZL P.11 was a Polish fighter aircraft that was introduced in 1934 and used during WWII by the Polish Air Force. At the start of the war the Polish Air Force had around 160 PZL P.11’s  available and for most parts they were no match to the modern aircraft used by the German Luftwaffe. A third of the PZL P.11’s were armed with four machine guns, but the rest only had two, and most of the aircraft were not equipped with a radio. Nevertheless the PZL P.11’s were better in many ways than their German counterparts, they were durable, had a good climb rate and could withstand high speed dives without risking breaking the wings off. The P.11 suffered heavy casualties during the defense of Poland in 1939 but did manage to shoot down a large number German aircraft, even though the exact number can not be verified. A total of 325 PZL P.11 were built, including a few variants.","faction":"Poland","type":"fighter","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":1,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":2},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_pzl_11","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_pzl_11_title","SourceString":"PZL P.11","LocalizedString":"PZL P.11"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::fighter","attack":1,"defense":2,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":1,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_pzl_11_text","SourceString":"Your Exile cards cost 1 less.","LocalizedString":"Your Exile cards cost 1 less."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_pzl_11_history","SourceString":"The PZL P.11 was a Polish fighter aircraft that was introduced in 1934 and used during WWII by the Polish Air Force. At the start of the war the Polish Air Force had around 160 PZL P.11’s  available and for most parts they were no match to the modern aircraft used by the German Luftwaffe. A third of the PZL P.11’s were armed with four machine guns, but the rest only had two, and most of the aircraft were not equipped with a radio. Nevertheless the PZL P.11’s were better in many ways than their German counterparts, they were durable, had a good climb rate and could withstand high speed dives without risking breaking the wings off. The P.11 suffered heavy casualties during the defense of Poland in 1939 but did manage to shoot down a large number German aircraft, even though the exact number can not be verified. A total of 325 PZL P.11 were built, including a few variants.","LocalizedString":"The PZL P.11 was a Polish fighter aircraft that was introduced in 1934 and used during WWII by the Polish Air Force. At the start of the war the Polish Air Force had around 160 PZL P.11’s  available and for most parts they were no match to the modern aircraft used by the German Luftwaffe. A third of the PZL P.11’s were armed with four machine guns, but the rest only had two, and most of the aircraft were not equipped with a radio. Nevertheless the PZL P.11’s were better in many ways than their German counterparts, they were durable, had a good climb rate and could withstand high speed dives without risking breaking the wings off. The P.11 suffered heavy casualties during the defense of Poland in 1939 but did manage to shoot down a large number German aircraft, even though the exact number can not be verified. A total of 325 PZL P.11 were built, including a few variants."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Uncommon","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Legions","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Passive","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardReset","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardSpawnedInHand","ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardDrawnFromDeck"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Exile"],"soundEnterPlay":{"ObjectName":"SoundCue'AU_depl_